{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrxHF4FbKyGr9HNNnBBJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The issue is fixed: `get_metadata_for_wheel()` now reads only `{dist}-{version}.dist-info/METADATA` for the wheel itself, so vendored `.dist-info` directories are ignored. Nothing is committed yet.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- **`src/fromager/pkgmetadata/pep376.py`** (new): `verbatim_dist_name()` and `dist_info_name()`. Both validate with `parse_wheel_filename`, so bad names or extensions raise `InvalidWheelFilename`. Both are exported from `fromager.pkgmetadata`.\n- **`src/fromager/candidate.py`**: `_wheel_metadata_path(url)` takes the last path segment, ignores query and fragment, and returns `dist_info_name(filename)/METADATA`. The fallback reads that one member and raises `ValueError` if it is missing.\n- **`src/fromager/wheels.py`**: `extract_info_from_wheel_file` uses `verbatim_dist_name`.\n- **`src/fromager/dependencies.py`**: `_get_metadata_from_wheel` uses `dist_info_name`, so no first-segment logic is left in that module.\n- **`tests/test_pep376.py`** (new): helper tests, `_wheel_metadata_path` tests, and fallback tests. The fallback test puts a vendored `.dist-info` first in the archive, which the old first-match loop would have returned.\n\n**Choices I made that you should check**\n\n- `dependencies.py` uses `dist_info_name` rather than `verbatim_dist_name` directly. The old code took the version from `parse_wheel_filename`'s normalized `Version`, so `Foo-1.0.RC1-…whl` produced `Foo-1.0rc1.dist-info`, which doesn't match the wheel's real directory. `dist_info_name` reuses `verbatim_dist_name` internally and fixes that case. It's covered by a regression test.\n- `_wheel_metadata_path` percent-decodes the filename, so `%2B` becomes `+` (as in `pkg-1.0+cpu`). The spec didn't mention this.\n- The \"not found\" message is unchanged, so existing matches on \"Could not find METADATA file\" still work.\n\n**Verification**\n\n- `tests/test_pep376.py`, `test_pep658_support.py`, `test_dependencies.py`, `test_wheels.py`, `test_pkgmetadata.py`, `test_bootstrapper.py`, `test_bootstrapper_iterative.py`, `test_resolver.py`, `test_sources.py`: 289 passed, 2 skipped, 1 failed.\n- The failure is `test_bootstrapper_iterative.py::TestPhasePrepareSource::test_constraint_logged_when_present`. The assertion is on a `caplog` log line from `bootstrapper.py`. That test patches out every function I changed. I did not run it against the pristine HEAD, so I can't say for certain it was already failing before my change.\n- `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` pass on the changed files. Ruff format reflowed one `raise` in `candidate.py`.\n- `mypy` was not run. It isn't in `.venv`, and the system copy fails with a missing module.\n- I did not run the full test suite, since CLAUDE.md asks for approval first.\n\n**Next step**\n\nNo commit has been made. Per your CLAUDE.md, I need you to approve the commit message before I run `git commit -s`. Let me know whether to commit, and whether you want the `dependencies.py` deviation kept."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4346,"cache_read_input_tokens":164363,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4346},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a9c11f82-5003-487d-9541-6d5566ffc276","uuid":"5b1daefe-c08b-48a4-b0ab-16145abab0c3","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:09:37.237Z","request_id":"req_011CfrxHEod9pcKHzhZE1k9v"}
