e assertion is on a `caplog` log line from `bootstrapper.py`. That test patches out every function I changed. I did not run it against the pristine HEAD, so I can't say for certain it was already failing before my change.\n- `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` pass on the changed files. Ruff format reflowed one `raise` in `candidate.py`.\n- `mypy` was not run. It isn't in `.venv`, and the system copy fails with a missing module.\n- I did not run the full test suite, since CLAUDE.md asks for approval first.\n\n**Next step**\n\nNo commit has been made. Per your CLAUDE.md, I need you to approve the commit message before I run `git commit -s`. Let me know whether to commit, and whether you want the `dependencies.py` deviation kept.", "ttft_ms": 986, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 159461, "uuid": "96da02c6-8eed-4ac3-b02c-1605517e16d7", "ttft_stream_ms": 721, "time_to_request_ms": 151, "first_content_frame_ms": 721, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0, "timestamp": "2026-10-09T16:09:37.292Z"}